{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And it shall come to pass, when it is completed.</b> He will finish, and like it: 'her hands shall complete' (Zechariah 4:9)." "<b>All his deed.</b> To bring the army of Sennacherib to Zion." "<b>Upon the fruit.</b> Like 'the fruit of their thoughts' (Jeremiah 6:19)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {2 "Ibn Ezra's lemma reads מחשבתו (singular 'his thought'), matching the Masoretic text of Isaiah 10:12; the marginal note צ״ל מחשבתם reflects the plural form found in the Jeremiah citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:53:13.258097048Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}